<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτι-επής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτιος, ἔπος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ready of speech, glib of tongue,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἐπίκλοπος ἔπλεο μύθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.281
				</span></i>
			: in good sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεφθέγξατο δ᾽
				ἀρτιεπής</span> answered <i>clearly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.61
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. γλῶσσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>I.</u>
					5(4).46
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
